 "notes": [
  "Requested Qal (\"bear witness\") excluded: zero attestations anywhere in the corpus. Attested stems are hiphil (dominant, 35 forms), piel (1), polel (2), hithpolel (1), hophal (1).",
  "Hiphil gloss trimmed from the requested \"testify; call to witness; warn\" to \"testify; warn\": \"testify\" and \"call to witness\" are the same evidenced sense worded twice (e.g. Deut.31.28, Deut.4.26 -- invoking heaven/earth as witnesses); \"warn\" is genuinely distinct (e.g. Exod.19.21, Neh.9.26/9.29 -- admonishing about consequences).",
  "Polel gloss changed from the requested \"restore\" to \"relieve\": both citations (Ps.146.9 \"relieves the fatherless and widow,\" Ps.147.6 \"lifts up the humble\") show sustaining/upholding someone in distress, not returning something to a former state. \"Restore\" isn't supported by either verse.",
  "Hithpolel (\"hithpalel\" in the original request) gloss changed from \"be restored\" to \"stand firm\": the one citation (Ps.20.9, וַנִּתְעוֹדָד) reads \"we have risen and stand upright/steady ourselves,\" not a restoration sense.",
  "Piel \"go around\" and hophal \"be warned\" matched their citations (Ps.119.61 \"the cords of the wicked have surrounded/entangled me\"; Exod.21.29 \"he had been warned\") as requested, no change."
 ],
 "stem_coverage_checked": true
